ill two copies remaining in the unshown tiles. Other tiles like B3 or F3 might be more valuable for potential melds or scoring.\nReason: Discarding T6 minimizes the risk of others completing their hands, while retaining flexibility for forming additional melds with the remaining T5, T7, and T8. Keeping B3 and F3 could aid in future pungs or scoring opportunities.\nAnswer: Play T6"}
